[b]Market–Average Relationship Engine[/b]

[b]What it does[/b]
Evaluates the relationship between price and one consistently selected moving average — the MA is treated as a market reference, not as a standalone crossover signal. Six diagnostic dimensions feed a bounded relationship oscillator and a set of confirmed events, so you can tell a healthy trend from an overextended one before you enter.

[b]Moving Average[/b]
[list]
[*]One family at a time: EMA, SMA, WMA, HMA, VWMA, RMA, DEMA, TEMA, ALMA — freely settable length and source
[*]No JMA — an unlicensed approximation would misrepresent the proprietary Jurik implementation
[/list]

[b]Six Diagnostic Scores (0-100)[/b]
[list]
[*]Trend — MA slope, price side, persistence of both, price efficiency, and direction agreement
[*]Respect — historical hit rate of price reactions around the MA, confidence-weighted by sample count
[*]Extension — ATR distance from the MA blended with statistical rarity vs. its own history
[*]Compression — share of recent bars near the MA plus ATR contraction
[*]Acceleration — separation velocity, MA-slope acceleration, and return acceleration
[*]Exhaustion — extension gated by efficiency decay, opposing wicks, stalled progress, and fading acceleration
[/list]

[b]Relationship Oscillator[/b]
[list]
[*]Signed −100..+100 line: Trend quality reduced by an Extension/Exhaustion quality penalty
[*]Extension and exhaustion degrade relationship quality but never flip its sign — a state can stay bullish while still flagging "Do Not Chase"
[*]Twelve-state classification: MA Compression, Healthy/Developing Bullish/Bearish, Bullish/Bearish Acceleration, Bullish/Bearish Do Not Chase, Bullish/Bearish Exhaustion Risk, Neutral/Unstructured
[/list]

[b]Confirmed Events[/b]
[list]
[*]PB — Pullback: trend + respect + prior extension + return to the MA zone + confirmed reaction candle + bounded exhaustion
[*]M — Momentum Release: breakout from prior MA compression with slope/acceleration/efficiency agreement
[*]! — Do Not Chase: extension crosses the risk threshold while the trend stays intact; not a reversal signal
[*]BR — Relationship Broken: sustained opposite-side acceptance plus a fading/reversing MA slope, not a single MA cross
[*]D — Divergence: price makes a lower low (higher high) while the relationship line makes a higher low (lower high) at the matching prior pivot — informational only, never gates the events above
[*]T — Turn From Extreme: the relationship line has recently touched a deep low/high and is now confirmed rising/falling off it, pivot-free — a new trend starting or an already-extended trend recognizably losing steam, depending on what preceded it
[*]Per-family signal cooldown to avoid re-triggering on the same move
[/list]

[b]Visuals & Diagnostics[/b]
[list]
[*]Optional MA line and event markers directly on the price chart alongside the oscillator pane, all kept small (`size.tiny`)
[*]Hover tooltips on every event marker with the full six-score readout, ATR distance, MA slope, and Respect sample count/hit rate
[*]All diagnostics additionally routed to the Data Window
[/list]

[b]Alerts[/b]
[list]
[*]Bullish/bearish Pullback, Momentum Release, Do Not Chase, and Exhaustion
[*]Bullish/bearish Relationship Broken, Divergence, and Turn From Extreme
[*]Combined "any MARE event" alert
[/list]

